{:event/actor "seb" :event/at #inst "2026-07-29T18:47:32.326Z" :event/body {:fact/path [:summary] :fact/value "UUID/nameUUIDFromBytes is UUID version 3 - MD5. Two issues. First, the input is the Message-ID, which the sender chooses freely, so anyone who can predict a Message-ID can pre-create that ticket; a later genuine message with the same id is then swallowed by already-have? as a duplicate, which is silent message suppression rather than a visible refusal. Second, MD5 in an identifier sits badly beside ADR 0006's one-algorithm-per-store hash policy and the sha256-everywhere discipline - chosen-prefix MD5 collisions are practical, so two crafted messages can be made to share a ticket. Derive the id from sha256 of the message-id (truncated into UUID shape) and treat an already-have? hit on a DIFFERENT sender as a reportable collision rather than a dup."} :event/parents #{"sha256-29c9a671c23d9328c5b9d1282c5b28b952a3eb691c3ade85b03e0198e63292d3"} :event/ticket #uuid "f21b781c-2076-48a8-9721-50399e5f5606" :event/type :fact/assert}